  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda Deaf Awareness and Communication (U-DAC) Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Deaf children and young people are often excluded from education because of their communication difficulties and because of a lack of belief in their abilities amongst their families and the wider community.  In Uganda, despite an enabling policy environment, scant resources are available for the inclusion of deaf children in ordinary schools, few teachers are equipped with positive attitudes towards deaf children or the skills to include them, and families and communities have generally assumed that deaf children cannot learn.  The project will work in three different districts in Uganda with an approach that has proved successful in Malawi where all three groups: community leaders; families and children; and teachers will receive training to help improve attitudes and develop local skills so that deaf children are able to go to school.  As a result many more deaf children and young people in these three districts will be able to achieve a good quality education.</narrative>
  </description>
